+/*
+ * begonia_usb.c (Loxy, 25 Nov 2026): USB device port for iOS on begonia (Redmi Note 8 Pro, MT6785).
+ *
+ * The USB-C port is wired to the MT6785 SSUSB IP (MediaTek "mtu3": device MAC at 0x11201000, IPPC at
+ * 0x11203e00, T-PHY at 0x11e40000; the board is USB 2.0 only). This driver runs it in device mode at
+ * high speed as one CDC-ACM serial port (IAD composite), which Windows 10/11 (usbser.sys), Linux
+ * (cdc_acm) and macOS bind without extra drivers:
+ *  - phone -> PC: the live kernel console (the sweet log ring, from its oldest byte) once the PC opens
+ *    the port (DTR set);
+ *  - PC -> phone: one-line commands, see usb_cmd() ("help" lists them).
+ * Polled from a kernel thread (1 ms while configured), PIO only: no QMU / DMA, so there is no memory
+ * the controller writes and nothing to keep cache coherent. The controller's level-1 interrupt output
+ * stays masked; the second-level status registers are polled.
+ *
+ * Sources: MediaTek's begonia 4.14 kernel (MiCode Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource begonia-r-oss)
+ * drivers/misc/mediatek/mu3d/hal (ssusb_*_c_header.h register map; mu3d_hal_usb_drv.c ssusb_en,
+ * rst_dev, dft_reg, ep_enable, write_fifo / read_fifo) and mu3d/drv/musb_gadget_ep0.c (SET_ADDRESS is
+ * written before SETUPPKTRDY | DATAEND), mu3phy/mt6785/mtk-phy-asic.c (phy_init_soc, usb_phy_recover);
+ * the EP0 state machine follows mainline drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_gadget_ep0.c. Clocks: infracfg_ao CG2
+ * bit 1 (INFRACFG_AO_USB_CG) and bit 31 (INFRACFG_AO_SSUSB_XHCI_CG), as the DT's mtu3_0 / usb3_phy
+ * nodes list them. The PHY's 3.3 V supply is MT6359 VUSB (LDO_VUSB_CON0 0x1d08, MON 0x1d0a).
+ *
+ * Boot-arg begoniausb=1 starts it (off by default until it has been seen working on the phone).
+ * Every log line starts with "BEGONIA USB:".
+ */
